 "notes": "Official model/code.py CodeNetMotionwithRot (net_dict key 'codewithrot', the paper's Body+Attitude model) instantiated with conf.propcov=True on CPU, torch.manual_seed(0), pypose stubbed (unused by the class). Official forward takes data['acc'], data['gyro'] as (B,T,3) in the BODY frame and concatenates [acc, gyro] (acc first) plus rot=(B,T,3) so(3) Log of the per-sample body-to-world attitude. The wrapper used for export maps IPB (B,6,T)=[gyro,acc] -> official order. total_params counts ALL registered parameters, including modules that the forward never uses (inherited self.cnn, fcn1, batchnorm1); see extra 'unused_params' and 'effective_params'. Parameter count does not depend on window length. Output is sequence-to-sequence: T_out = floor((floor((T-1)/3)+1-1)/3)+1 (23 for T=200, 112 for T=1000); cov = exp(decoder - 5) is a per-axis VARIANCE (not logstd).",
